            <span style="font-size:8px;">
                (Indexed to !}
                [+ economic_year +]
                {! GDP)
            </span>
        </div>!}
    {!</div>!}

{!</div>!}
]

Government Economic Policy : [+ economic_direction +]

[? if economic_direction == 'Douglas Model' : Current [+ party_names.ccf +] policy is to continue Douglas' approach of mixing state ownership, co-operatives, and private enterprise in a pragmatic manner, attempting to maintain the province's economic growth while producing a mixed economic outlook tailored to Saskatchewan needs. ?]

[? if economic_direction == 'Returning to Phelps' : After much intra-party struggle, Joe Phelps' state-directed economic policy is back on the board. Necessarily, this means an expansion of Crown Corporations, particularly in the mineral and manfuacturing sectors which the Douglas administration largely left to private business. ?]

[? if economic_direction == 'Inducing Enterprise' : [+ party_names.ccf +] has undergone another significant moderation in an attempt to attract private capital into the province. Private industry has already had a strong foothold in the mineral sector of Alberta and manufacturing sector of Manitoba. Perhaps this could be a harbinger of good things to come. ?]

- @attract_industry
- @cooperative_technical_aid
- @cooperative_financial_aid
- @housing_finance
- @return_phelps
- @crown_pulp_mill

@housing_finance
title: Financing Housing
subtitle: Provide low-interest loans, loan guarantees, and other financial assistance for home construction and renovation 

@attract_industry
title: Incentivizing Industrial Development
subtitle: Attract private industry in secondary sectors by issuing generous grants and loans through the [? if year <= 1962 : Industrial Development Office ?][? if year > 1962 : Saskatchewan Economic Development Corporation ?] <br>This will aid in the development of IPSCO and the Saskatchewan Cement Corporation 

@cooperative_technical_aid
title: Aiding Cooperatives
subtitle: Provide further technical and operational assistance to developing cooperatives

@cooperative_financial_aid
title: Aiding Cooperatives
subtitle: Provide generous grants and loans to developing and established cooperatives to expand the cooperative influence in the provincial economy



@douglas_model
style: gov-scene



@return_phelps
style: gov-scene


@sask_mineral_expansion
title: Expand Saskatchewan Mineral (CC) Production
subtitle: Saskatchewan Minerals so far has been a relatively minor operation; Begin constructing a sodium sulphate plant at Ingebrigt under the Sask Minerals name

@crown_pulp_mill
title: A Crown Pulp Mill
subtitle: The Douglas government was unable to find a business-case for a Pulp Mill; give Saskatchewan Forest Products (CC) a mandate to construct a pulp mill north of Prince Albert 

@sask_oil
title: Establish the Saskatchewan Oil and Gas Corporation
subtitle: Party membership calls for a government-owned oil and gas (CC); Establish a Crown Corporation to involve itself in the exploration and production of O&G